316:%Suppose $\C$ is an $\FF_{q_0}$-linear MRD-code with parameters $[n^2,nk,n-k+1]$. Then $\C^{\perp}$ is a linear MRD-code with parameters $[n^2,n(n-k),k+1]$. Moreover, $\C$ is equivalent to $\C'$ if and only if $\C^{\perp}$ is equivalent to $\C'^{\perp}$.
