327:\section{Construction of new linear MRD-codes}
330:\begin{lemma}
332:Suppose $f$ is a linearized polynomial of $q$-degree $k$. If $f$ has rank $n-k$, then $N(f_0) = (-1)^{kn}N(f_k)$.
336:For any $k$-dimensional $\Fq$-subspace $U$ of $\Fqn$, there is a unique monic linearized polynomial of $q$-degree $k$ that annihilates $U$ (that is, contains $U$ in its set of roots). We denote this by $m_U$ and call it the minimal polynomial of $U$,. Every linearized polynomial of degree $k$ annihilating $U$ is an $\Fqn$-multiple of $m_U$, and hence it suffices to prove the result for any particular linearized polynomial of degree $k$ annihilating $U$.
