351:\begin{theorem}
352:Let $\HH_k(\eta,h)$ denote the set of linearized polynomials of $q$-degree at most $k\leq n-1$ satisfying $f_k = \eta f_0^{q^h}$, with $\eta$ such that $N(\eta) \ne (-1)^{nk}$, i.e.
356:Then each $\HH_k(\eta,h)$ is an MRD-code with the same parameters as $\G_k$. 
360:It is clear that $\HH_k(\eta,h)$ has dimension $nk$ over $\Fq$. As $\deg(f) \leq q^k$ for all $f\in \HH_k(\eta,h)$, we have that $\rank(f) \geq n-k$. By Lemma \ref{lem:coeffs}, $\rank(f) >n-k$, and hence $\rank(f) \geq n-k+1$ for all $f\in \HH_k(\eta,h)$. It follows that $\HH_k(\eta,h)$ is an MRD-code with parameters $[n^2,nk,n-k+1]$, as claimed.
