codex
A viable family is emerging from Section 3’s exact duality theorem, and it is honestly Track B. The solver will receive a twisted Gabidulin code over \(\mathrm{GF}(3^n)\) in a normal basis and must give the compact twist vector of its Delsarte dual. Generic dual-code construction expands an \(nk \times n^2\) generator and computes a nullspace; the paper’s trace/Frobenius adjunction reduces the answer to one cyclic coordinate shift and a sign change. I’m using a normal basis so that the compact route stays exact and under 300 operations rather than becoming a disguised CAS exercise.
