codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on Theorems 5–6 of the [paper’s MRD construction](https://arxiv.org/html/1504.01581v2#S3).

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1504.01581/gen_1504_01581.py:20)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1504.01581/selftest_report.json)
- [README and audit](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1504.01581/README.md:1)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1504.01581/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1504.01581/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1504.01581/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results pass G1–G9(c): 12/12 planted and norm checks, 0/200,000 random hits, five attacks at 0/8, reference solver 8/8 at 1,711,839 operations, and 80/80 canonicalization checks.

The only unresolved requirement is STEP 4: all 12 OpenRouter requests returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” before inference. The result is therefore documented accurately but is not submission-ready until the three hardening runs can obtain real oracle verdicts.
